# Phase 6, chunk A4: a user may remove their own suppressions, and the removal is a WRITE the gate must keep confined like the insert (internal/suppress Remove, which validates the address first, is the only place
# that removes a row: the history is written by the table's own trigger, but the Go validator is still the only wall for the two punycode shapes the CHECK cannot see). The fault adds a second non-test Go file
# under internal/ that holds a raw string with a DELETE FROM platform.suppressions and never calls the validator; the gate must name the file and the line and say the write is outside the sanctioned writer, and
# name the kind (DELETE FROM). The control side is the real repository, which must be green. Needs bash only: no database, no module, no Go.
# The patch adds a new file, so it depends on no committed file; the control needs internal/suppress/store.go, scripts/check-suppression-writers.sh and tests/suppression-writer-exceptions.txt at HEAD.
GATE=suppression-delete-writer
TARGET=platform
SETUP=
STEP=check-suppression-writers on the real repository
CMD=bash scripts/check-suppression-writers.sh
MESSAGE=internal/app/zz_suppression_delete_writer.go:4: write to platform.suppressions (DELETE FROM) outside the sanctioned writer internal/suppress/store.go
MESSAGE=check-suppression-writers: RED
